# Clippy RAM

Hard caps (not agent-only):

- `~/.cargo/config.toml` and this repo's `.cargo/config.toml` set `[build] jobs = 2`. Cargo, rust-analyzer, Homebrew, and rustup all honor that.
- `~/.local/bin/cargo` forces `cargo clippy --jobs 2` and strips a higher `-j` from the caller.
- GitHub CI sets `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS` to raise the cap on the runner.

Do not run `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets` on a developer machine at full parallelism. Prefer `cargo clippy -p <crate> -- -D warnings`. rust-analyzer stays on `cargo check`; never set `rust-analyzer.check.command` to `clippy` or `rust-analyzer.cargo.features` to `"all"`.
